<title>FINLAND: Foreign ownership in Finnish companies up in Jan.</title>
<headline>Foreign ownership in Finnish companies up in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign ownership of Finnish firms registered in the Central Share Register (OKR) rose to 27.2 percent of shares at end-January from 26.9 percent at end-1996, OKR said in a review received on Thursday.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership in telecom group Nokia was up to 71.40 percent at end-January from 70.66 percent at end-December, OKR said.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership of food, animal feed and chemicals group Raision Tehtaat rose to 52.46 percent from 50.87 percent and foreign holdings in media group Aamulehti rose to 49.11 percent from 42.45 percent.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership in pharmaceuticals wholesaler Tamro fell to 50.89 percent from 53.32 percent at the end of last year.</p>
<p>Foreign holdings in compass maker Suunto fell to 18.88 percent at end-January from 22.64 percent at end-December, OKR said.  </p>
